From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bernardo Pereira <bpereira@cloudflare.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 09:16:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Let stylo invalidate a removed stylesheet instead of forcing
 every origin

Removing a <style> element called force_stylesheet_origins_dirty for all
origins after Stylist::remove_stylesheet had already collected the sheet's
selector invalidations. That rebuilt the UA, user and author cascade data and
put a full restyle on the root, so a page that adds and removes a temporary
<Style> (next-themes' disableTransitionOnChange) recascaded the whole document
on every toggle: 29 ms per getComputedStyle read on hashnode.com.

Stylo's own removal path invalidates what the sheet matched and falls back to a
full invalidation for universal selectors and untargetable rules, so dropping
the extra call keeps behaviour and removes the redundant work.
---
 src/mutator.rs | 7 ++++---
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/mutator.rs b/src/mutator.rs
index f5ad587..89387bd 100644
--- a/src/mutator.rs
+++ b/src/mutator.rs
@@ -1984,12 +1984,13 @@ impl<'doc> DocumentMutator<'doc> {
                 self.doc.remove_shadow_stylesheet(shadow_root_id, stylesheet);
             }
             None => {
+                // Stylo collects the removed sheet's selector invalidations itself
+                // (and falls back to a full invalidation for rules it cannot
+                // target). Forcing every origin dirty here recascaded the whole
+                // document on each <style> removal.
                 let guard = self.doc.guard.read();
                 self.doc.stylist.remove_stylesheet(stylesheet, &guard);
                 drop(guard);
-                self.doc
-                    .stylist
-                    .force_stylesheet_origins_dirty(OriginSet::all());
             }
         }
         self.doc.stylesheet_generation += 1;
